  "narrative": "No new independent validation was delivered and no claims are under a response deadline; the independent-validation quota is exhausted. I therefore registered no new comparisons and closed the remaining active diagnostic claims as investigation status only: H35 is accepted and closed as the mature central finding, while H43, H62, and H142 remain unresolved but closed because no available validation or adequately powered follow-up can resolve them within this dataset and remaining workflow. The conclusions below are dataset-specific associations, not causal or externally generalizable findings.\n\nThe central supported finding is that feature_065=1 versus feature_065=0 is associated with stronger outcome_013 dependency. Under the registered negative direction, a positive signed estimate means the exposed group has more negative dependency scores. H35 discovery R29 estimated +0.117 (95% CI 0.082 to 0.152), and independent validation R39 estimated +0.132 (independent CI 0.080 to 0.184). These effects are far above the operational 10% benchmark applied earlier, approximately 0.027 for outcome_013. Replicated accepted contrasts in feature_008=1, feature_060=1 and 0, feature_043 above and below 8, feature_045=1 and 0, feature_061>=54, and especially clean feature_027=0 strata including age subsets support a common feature_065-outcome_013 association in the cleaner population. This is a measured marker, not a biological mechanism.\n\nA second robust dataset-specific result is feature_027=1 versus feature_027=0 on outcome_014. H116 discovery R116 estimated +0.796 (CI 0.776 to 0.816), and validation R118 estimated +0.781 (independent CI 0.752 to 0.809). Accepted subset analyses H127 and H130 replicate the magnitude. This is enormous relative to the outcome_014 scale and, with H222 showing no comparable outcome_005 shift, is best interpreted as an outcome_014-specific coding, leakage, scale, missing-data, or data-structure artifact rather than biology.\n\nNegative and unsupported findings are also important. Feature_060, feature_002, feature_054, feature_045, feature_020, feature_063, and most other tested binary or categorical predictors do not provide secure clinically meaningful dependency shifts. Several discovery leads were weakened or reversed by validation: feature_060/outcome_006 H3 R13 is weak, feature_054/outcome_006 H20 R79 is null, interaction H26 R26 is null, feature_063/outcome_014 subgroup H55 R92 reverses the claimed direction, feature_020/outcome_006 H114/H117 R130 is null, and feature_027/outcome_013 H118 R143 does not reproduce the discovery estimate. Feature_065 does not securely extend to outcome_005 or most other outcomes; H230 and H62 remain unresolved with small clean-stratum estimates. There is no secure second outcome_013 marker: clean-stratum screens H218 and H219 are rejected and H220 is unresolved. The broad feature_065 stability screen across nominal categories H223 through H229 did not support clinically meaningful effect modification in the registered directions; H224 rejects a claimed feature_019 interaction, and H225/H226 are identical redundant tests that should not be double counted.\n\nThe main unresolved uncertainty is feature_065 behavior in feature_027=1 and other small or artifact-prone subgroups. H142 and H233 remain uncertain because feature_027=1 cells are small. H231 rejects the claimed stronger feature_065 effect in feature_027=1 relative to its complement; the signed pattern suggests attenuation, but no adequately powered reverse or attenuation test is available, so attenuation is a cautionary observation rather than an accepted subgroup effect. H79 is also unresolved and its validation R78 is close to null, so it is less mature than H35, H49, H51, and the accepted clean feature_027=0 age replicates. H53 in feature_008=0 remains small and imprecise despite an interval-supported discovery estimate. The cause of the feature_027/outcome_014 anomaly remains unresolved.\n\nThe most informative next analysis is not additional subgroup fishing. It is a data-integrity audit of feature_027/outcome_014, including raw value distributions, coding, missingness, batch or source structure, scale transformations, and possible leakage, followed by external or independent validation of the feature_065/outcome_013 association if available. If only internal work could continue, the single most useful pre-specified test would be a properly powered attenuation or reverse interaction test of feature_065 by feature_027 for outcome_013, explicitly labeled diagnostic rather than biological. Overall, the evidence supports one robust measured marker of stronger outcome_013 dependency, feature_065, primarily in clean feature_027=0 evidence; it also identifies feature_027 as a cautionary diagnostic variable and does not support a broad second marker or a generalized cross-outcome dependency axis.",
  "research_notes": "Final synthesis, iteration 19. No new validation released; no response-deadline assessments due; validation quota exhausted. Registered no new comparisons. Closed active investigation status: H35 accepted and closed as mature central finding; H43, H62, and H142 remain unresolved but closed because further subgroup testing would be post-hoc or low-powered without new external evidence.\n\nCentral supported dataset-specific finding: feature_065=1 versus 0 predicts stronger outcome_013 dependency. H35 discovery R29 +0.117 CI 0.082 to 0.152; validation R39 +0.132 independent CI 0.080 to 0.184; operational outcome_013 threshold about 0.027. Positive signed estimate for direction -1 means more negative dependency. Accepted replicates across feature_008=1, feature_060=1 and 0, feature_043 above/below 8, feature_045=1 and 0, feature_061>=54, and clean feature_027=0 strata including age subsets. Interpretation is association only, not causality or generalizability.\n\nRobust diagnostic artifact: feature_027=1 versus 0 produces huge outcome_014 shift. H116 R116 +0.796 CI 0.776 to 0.816; validation R118 +0.781 independent CI 0.752 to 0.809; clean-stratum H127/H130 replicate. H222 outcome_005 is small/unresolved, supporting an outcome_014-specific artifact rather than global feature_027 dependency axis. Audit feature_027/outcome_014 for coding, leakage, scale, missingness, or batch structure before any biological interpretation.\n\nNegative/unsupported findings: feature_060, feature_002, feature_054, feature_045, feature_020, feature_063, and most binary/categorical predictors lack clinically meaningful secure association. Validation weakened or reversed many leads: H3 R13, H20 R79, H26 R26, H55 R92, H114/H117 R130, H118 R143. No secure feature_065 extension to outcome_005: H230 unresolved, H62 closed unresolved. No secure second outcome_013 marker: H218/H219 rejected, H220 unresolved. Feature_065 stability interactions H223-H229 did not support clinically meaningful registered effect modification; H224 rejected claimed feature_019 interaction; H225/H226 identical redundant and should not be double-counted.\n\nUnresolved caution: feature_065 within feature_027=1 remains uncertain due small cells; H142/H233 unresolved. H231 rejects claimed stronger feature_065 interaction in feature_027=1; signed pattern suggests attenuation but not accepted. H79 unresolved with validation R78 near null; not as mature as accepted clean-stratum age replicates. H53 feature_008=0 small and imprecise. Some feature_061 and feature_045 interaction contrasts remain wide.\n\nNext most informative analysis: data-integrity audit of feature_027/outcome_014 and external/independent validation of feature_065/outcome_013. If internal only, a pre-specified attenuated/reversed feature_065-by-feature_027 interaction test with adequate power is the only useful next diagnostic analysis. Avoid further subgroup fishing. Final conclusion: feature_065 is a robust measured outcome_013 dependency marker mainly in clean feature_027=0 evidence; feature_027 is a cautionary diagnostic variable; no broad cross-outcome dependency axis or secure second marker is supported."
